menu "Aquila firmware OTA"

    config AQUILA_OTA_HEALTH_WINDOW_S
        int "Pending-verify health window (seconds)"
        default 60
        range 1 3600
        help
            After an OTA image activates, the node must stay healthy
            (associated, streaming CSI, control responsive) for this many
            seconds before it calls esp_ota_mark_app_valid_cancel_rollback().
            If it does not confirm, the bootloader rolls back to the previous
            image (docs/spec/firmware-ota.md §6).

    config AQUILA_FW_SECURITY_VERSION
        int "Compiled-in firmware security-version floor"
        default 0
        range 0 2147483647
        help
            The anti-rollback floor this build enforces. The effective floor is
            the greater of this value and the monotonic value persisted in NVS
            after a successful update; an OTA image whose version encodes a
            lower security version is rejected (firmware-ota.md §4).

    config AQUILA_FW_ALLOW_DOWNGRADE
        bool "Allow a factory-authorised downgrade below the floor"
        default n
        help
            The explicit factory-authorised force flag of firmware-ota.md §4.
            When disabled (the default), the node rejects any image below the
            security-version floor.

    config AQUILA_FW_PUBKEY_HEX
        string "Compiled-in Ed25519 firmware public key (64 hex characters)"
        default ""
        help
            The 32-byte Ed25519 trust anchor, as 64 hex characters. A key
            provisioned in NVS under the `ota` namespace, key `fw_pubkey`,
            takes precedence. When neither is set the node has no trust anchor
            and fails every OTA verification closed.

endmenu
